7. POWER AUTOMATE STATUS
==================================================

Flow name:
- Activity Log Processing

Overall intended structure:
1. Trigger: SharePoint - When an item is created
2. First Update item action:
   - Workflow Status = In Progress
   - Excel Logged = No
   - pass through the rest of the required fields
3. First Condition:
   - When an item is created -> Activity Type Value
   - equals Direct Service
   - True -> Add row to Direct_Hours
   - False -> go to second condition
4. Second Condition:
   - When an item is created -> Activity Type Value
   - equals Indirect Service
   - True -> Add row to Indirect_Hours
   - False -> Add row to Supervision
5. Final Update item in each branch:
   - Workflow Status = Complete
   - Excel Logged = Yes

Important Power Automate corrections already discovered:
- Conditions must use:
  - When an item is created -> Activity Type Value
- Right-side comparison text must be exact choice text:
  - Direct Service
  - Indirect Service
- Table names are not used in the conditions
- Table names are used only in the Excel actions:
  - Direct_Hours
  - Indirect_Hours
  - Supervision

